## The Setting Stack

The Setting Stack is the framework for building your total ring price without overspending. One number. Two line items. No surprises.

Your Total Ring Number is one figure: stone price plus setting price. That is your ring. Set this total before you do anything else.

Most buyers find a stone they love, then add the setting as a second expense. That is how budgets overrun. Set the total first, then allocate it.

**The split for radiant cut:** 75–80% on the stone, 20–25% on the setting. The stone does all the visual work — 70 facets, brilliance, size. A [Petite Solitaire at $1,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-195639?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is not a compromise — it is the correct allocation.

Spending $3,000 on a setting for a stone under 2ct natural is the wrong call. The setting does not create the fire. The stone does.

